{"id":3,"createdAt":"2026-05-14T23:27:37.385Z","runId":"vfy-mp64c0by-vqln","runKind":"verify","domainName":"blocks-world","isCustomDomain":false,"savedDomainId":null,"transformerHash":null,"rendererHash":null,"llmProvider":"claude","stateIndex":1,"totalStates":5,"extractorModelId":"claude-sonnet-4-5","extractorVersion":"unvis-v1","imageHash":"b15a9d17b87c45ca273a2b77d0ddd342893b76db145dd17058eb67734a9a6fcd","imagePath":null,"expected":["(clear a)","(clear c)","(holding b)","(ontable a)","(ontable c)"],"extracted":["(ontable a)","(ontable c)","(clear a)","(clear c)","(holding b)"],"scope":["clear","holding","ontable"],"tp":["(clear a)","(clear c)","(holding b)","(ontable a)","(ontable c)"],"fp":[],"fn":[],"precision":1,"recall":1,"parseFailure":false,"rawText":"I'll analyze the image to identify the ground predicates that hold in this blocks-world state.\n\n**Analysis:**\n\nFrom the image, I can see:\n- Block A (red/pink) is on the table\n- Block C (blue) is on the table\n- Block B (cyan/turquoise) is being held by the gripper (shown suspended above with gripper lines)\n\n**Mapping to predicates:**\n\n1. **ontable**: Block A is on the table, Block C is on the table\n   - `(ontable a)`\n   - `(ontable c)`\n\n2. **clear**: Block A has nothing on top of it, Block C has nothing on top of it\n   - `(clear a)`\n   - `(clear c)`\n\n3. **holding**: The gripper is holding Block B\n   - `(holding b)`\n\n4. **handempty**: The hand is NOT empty (it's holding B), so this predicate does NOT hold\n\n5. **on**: No block is on top of another block\n\nPREDICATES_JSON: [\"(ontable a)\", \"(ontable c)\", \"(clear a)\", \"(clear c)\", \"(holding b)\"]","feedbackId":null,"humanLabeller":null,"imageProvenance":null}
{"id":4,"createdAt":"2026-05-14T23:28:07.373Z","runId":"vfy-mp64c0by-vqln","runKind":"verify","domainName":"blocks-world","isCustomDomain":false,"savedDomainId":null,"transformerHash":null,"rendererHash":null,"llmProvider":"claude","stateIndex":3,"totalStates":5,"extractorModelId":"claude-sonnet-4-5","extractorVersion":"unvis-v1","imageHash":"8b899c3d9a60637a505591b5d0dc51a889a2e81dfa3766d3260ba75a33588059","imagePath":null,"expected":["(clear b)","(holding c)","(on b a)","(ontable a)"],"extracted":["(ontable a)","(on b a)","(clear b)","(holding c)"],"scope":["clear","holding","on","ontable"],"tp":["(clear b)","(holding c)","(on b a)","(ontable a)"],"fp":[],"fn":[],"precision":1,"recall":1,"parseFailure":false,"rawText":"I'll analyze the image to identify the ground predicates that hold in this blocks-world state.\n\n**Analysis:**\n\nFrom the image, I can see:\n1. Block A (pink/red) is on the table\n2. Block B (teal/cyan) is on top of block A\n3. Block C (blue) is being held by the gripper (shown suspended with a line above it)\n\n**Mapping to predicates:**\n\n- Block A is on the table: `(ontable a)`\n- Block B is on block A: `(on b a)`\n- Block B has nothing on top of it: `(clear b)`\n- Block C is being held by the gripper: `(holding c)`\n- The hand is NOT empty (it's holding C), so `(handempty)` does NOT hold\n\nNote: Block A is not clear because B is on it. Block C is being held, so it's neither on anything nor on the table, and it is not clear in the traditional sense (though one might argue a held block is \"clear\" - but since it's held, we focus on the holding predicate).\n\nPREDICATES_JSON: [\"(ontable a)\", \"(on b a)\", \"(clear b)\", \"(holding c)\"]","feedbackId":null,"humanLabeller":null,"imageProvenance":null}
